    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d476">

                <pb facs="0570" n="482" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg482"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Clayton to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1904-03-01"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March 1, 1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2173.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to former correspondence relating
                    to the case of Conductor L. C. Crutcher,<anchor n="a" xml:id="d476-f1"/> I now
                    have the honor to transmit a copy of correspondence between the embassy and Jose
                    Lopez Moctezuma, local attorney of the Mexican Central Railway Company, from
                    which it will be seen that the superior tribunal of the State of San Luis Potosi
                    has confirmed the decision of the court of first instance, by which Mr. Crutcher
                    is relieved of all responsibility.</p>
                <p>As at present advised, I conclude that no further action in this case is required
                    by the embassy.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Powell Clayton.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d476-a1.xml" xpointer="d476-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
